# peeryard patch ergo/008: Drop a requested copy of a modifier already in history instead of penalizing the sender
# upstream: ergoplatform/ergo#2592 (proposed); origin, witness and responses in patches.json
commit 5aa282449551cab394bb70ea25db76e3dd1f1b77
Author: cafebedouin <cafebedouin@gmail.com>
Date:   Fri Oct 16 14:33:52 2026 -0500

    Spec: penalty checks print what was sent; the extension test reuses historyWithNewHeader
    
    - replyForHeldModifier and the ADProofs test check sent.collect { case p: PenalizePeer => p } shouldBe empty, so a
      failure shows the penalty and the peer.
    - The extension test held one section in a Seq; it now uses historyWithNewHeader, as the block transactions test
      does, and handles the extension directly.
    - historyWithNewHeader takes the fixture's viewHistory (since #2591) instead of asking the view holder again.
    - The ADProofs test drops an @SuppressWarnings for wartremover, which is not in the build.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

